      "jobId": "26e0564e-1e2c-4e2d-9bb4-434a281784c6",
      "question": "Among the 50 most liquid US stocks, which had the strongest and weakest returns over the 20 trading sessions ending March 12, 2026, and how did their daily volatility compare?",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-01T04:40:50.697989Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-01T04:41:32.206261Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "**Top‑50 most liquid U.S. stocks – 20‑session window ending 2026‑03‑12**\n\n| Position | Ticker | 20‑session return | Daily volatility (σ) |\n|----------|--------|-------------------|----------------------|\n| Strongest (rank 1) | **CRCL** | **+97.37 %** | **8.86 %** |\n| Weakest (rank 1)   | **BABA** | **‑18.45 %** | **1.79 %** |\n\n*Returns and volatilities are expressed as percentages (the tools return fractions; 0.9737 → 97.37 %).*\n\n- **CRCL** posted the highest cumulative return (+97.37 %) over the 20 trading sessions, but its daily price swings were relatively large (σ ≈ 8.86 %).\n- **BABA** had the lowest return (‑18.45 %) and exhibited much calmer daily movement (σ ≈ 1.79 %).\n\n**Limitations** – The figures are descriptive historical observations from the market‑data pack; they are not investment advice.\n\n[1]\n[2]\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Market analytics result — market scan — evidence `hermes-receipt:db6830cd34ab59814f988fff56a87aa7e90f93afbba6e1b7d33563c4193cc8b7`\n- [2] Market analytics result — market scan — evidence `hermes-receipt:0c11181c730c037a76b3b8f429a8f8e26e623c8fc78a38d9f8fe9f6054df38d3`",
